# 5.1.prepare.stone

## .what

write the preparation sheet: what to carry, what to ask, what to expect. this turns the ranked
referral into an actionable step for the patient — the difference between a name on a list and a
visit that goes well.

## .inputs

- `1.1.intake.need.yield.md` — the specialty + the case context
- `4.1.access.rank.yield.md` — the ranked options (the likely venue shapes the prep)

## .do

- **what to carry** — the concrete items the visit needs (e.g. photos of the lesion over time, a
  list of current medications, insurance/coverage details, prior records if any)
- **what to ask** — the questions that make the visit count (e.g. "is this consistent with X?",
  "do i need a biopsy?", "what change means i should come back sooner?")
- **what to expect** — the shape of the visit for the likely venue (a telederm store-and-forward
  flow vs an in-person exam), so the patient is not surprised
- keep it venue-aware: a telederm prep differs from an in-person prep (photo quality matters more)

## .emit

into `5.1.prepare.yield.md` — the three sections (carry, ask, expect), venue-aware.

## .done when

the carry / ask / expect sections are written, concrete, and matched to the likely venue from the
top-ranked option.
